## Context

Author decision (Imagine, 2026-11-09, session in `~/CNRS/missions`, after
the naming round that settled `/paper` (1483) and `/mission` (1485)):
a third object skill, `/post`, for the blog post and the op-ed
(tribune). Same naming rule: a skill that manages an object of the trade
carries the object's name. `post` is the word of WordPress and of HAL's
doctype BLOG, understood in French, one syllable; `billet` excludes the
op-ed, `tribune` excludes the post, `piece` is vague. No `posts/`
directory exists: posts live in the carnet's repo, op-eds where they are
born (often a mission folder), so the name designates the object, not a
directory.

Queued behind `/paper` and `/mission`: its common trunk reuses what those
two write (section skeleton, provenance step, `/update-publist` gates,
roadmap row).

Evidence that a skill is missing: the same landing exists in two copies.
- Blog posts: `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/realf.hypotheses.org/AGENTS.md`,
  « Procedure, once per billet » (Markdown source of truth, companion PDF
  via pandoc/xelatex with the shared `header-includes.tex`, HAL SWORD
  deposit in doctype BLOG, `@misc` in `Ha-Duong.bib`, download line added
  to the post through the WordPress REST API, `journal.md` and
  `backlog.md` lines). About two hundred lines, local to the carnet.
- Op-ed: the Jéco 2026 tribune « Transition électrique, qui porte le
  risque » landed the same way (page `@misc`, HAL hal-05847469) through a
  one-off pipeline rebuilt by hand in
  `~/CNRS/missions/actif/2026-11-03 Jéco/release/2026-11-01/publication/`
  and `output/pdf/build_tribune.py`.

## Design

- `skills/post/SKILL.md` is a short router: argument `<post> <stage>`,
  stage ∈ `draft | publish | archive`; it resolves the post's folder
  (carnet `billets/<AAAA-MM-JJ slug>/` or a mission folder), reads the
  project's AGENTS.md if any, then loads `references/<stage>.md`.
- `references/draft.md`: delegates only, `/message-framing` then
  `/cut-prose`; the carnet's editorial rules (language per post, dragon
  metaphor, red line on CNRS-funded results, declassification of
  incidents) are read from `backlog.md`, not copied.
- `references/publish.md`: one section per channel, each naming who
  clicks. Carnet: the WordPress REST recipe stays in the carnet's
  AGENTS.md, the checklist points at it and lists the gates (draft
  status, category and tags, preview, publication is the author's
  gesture). Newspaper or partner site: the editor publishes; the
  checklist records the sent version, the published version and the
  diff between them (provenance).
- `references/archive.md`, the common trunk: companion PDF from the
  Markdown source, never from the rendered page; human validation of
  the PDF; HAL deposit (doctype BLOG for a post, OTHER for an op-ed
  unless the venue fits better) and `@misc` on the page through
  `/update-publist`; back-link from the live post to the PDF (REST API
  for the carnet, nothing for a newspaper); roadmap row in
  « Communications »; dated `release/<AAAA-MM-JJ>/` subfolder with the
  authentic artifacts, hashed; for a carnet post, lines in `journal.md`
  and `backlog.md`.
- Each checklist carries the six sections of `/paper` and `/mission`:
  registers touched, provenance step, filesystem steps, outward gates
  with who clicks, delegates, author-only items.
- The carnet's AGENTS.md keeps its WordPress and HAL recipes: they are
  specific to that site and that gabarit. The skill carries the trunk and
  the routing, and the AGENTS.md gains one line pointing at `/post`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `skills/post/SKILL.md` router and three checklists in
      `skills/post/references/`, catalog updated, hygiene tests pass
- [ ] Each checklist carries the six sections shared with `/paper` and
      `/mission`
- [ ] `/post "2026-11-06 The client the contractor and 18 agents" archive`
      dry run reproduces the carnet's procedure steps 1–7 and leaves
      nothing for the agent to discover
- [ ] `/post <Jéco tribune> archive` dry run lands on « nothing to do
      except the roadmap check » (positive control: already on page and
      HAL)
- [ ] The carnet's AGENTS.md points at `/post` in one line, its recipes
      unchanged
- [ ] `make check` passes
